extraction_notes: "WB9 South America 2 printed 77-79 (cache p077-p079, page_offset 0); the lore opens on 77, abilities and the stat block are on 78, the list ends on 79. Printed 78 read off a 110 dpi render: the OCR''s ''W.d to Hand: Martial Arts'' is printed that way in the book itself, a typo for Hand to Hand: Martial Arts, and the Rogue line reads ''(+5%0'' in print too. No fallam-battlemaster class was in production on 2026-09-25. || XP: the Duelist, Fallam Battlemaster and Rune Warrior ladder on printed 192, read off a render, stored as given; in a pairing it wins over the race''s. || GROUP: men-of-arms - an elite warrior class, in The Arkhons section of the book with no group heading. No sdc_base or mdc_base is printed; men_of_arms: true is stated because every O.C.C. with neither pool must carry the line, read as a warrior (the inca-warrior precedent for a warrior O.C.C. under a section with no group heading). It can only matter played without the race, which race_restrictions forbids; the race''s mdc_base always applies. || RACE: the attribute requirements say open to the Fallam R.C.C. only; stored as race_restrictions only fallam. Written as the ADDITION to that race (the pucara-mind-mage shape): attribute dice, M.D.C., P.P.E., Horror Factor, the race''s bonuses and natural abilities come from the R.C.C. and are not restated, because bonuses, special_abilities, natural_abilities and equipment are summed across a pairing. || ATTRIBUTES: requirements P.S. 22 and P.P. 16. Ability 1''s +2 P.S., +1 P.P., +1D4 P.E. and +1D4x10 M.D.C. stored as bonuses (attributes and pools; the P.E. and M.D.C. dice are rolled once). || BONUSES: ability 2''s +1 initiative, +1 strike, parry and dodge and +1 attack per melee stored unconditionally. Every Battle Trance bonus is conditional on the trance and is prose (the Battle Trance ability); its after-effects are side_effects. The trance has no uses-per-day limit, so no trackable_resources. || SKILLS: Language and Literacy: Arkhon (98%) restated as Language: Arkhon 98 and Literacy: Native Language 98, the race''s own reading (held once across the pairing). The Earth language of choice (+15%) is the same CHOICE group the race grants and is NOT restated, since choice groups from both halves are not merged and restating it would give two. Basic Radio is Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55; the race''s 60 is the higher base and is the one held. Prowl 25+15, Detect Ambush 30+15, Wilderness Survival 30+10, W.P. Sword, W.P. Energy Rifle. Hand to Hand: Martial Arts is granted and replaces the race''s Basic (a later grant wins). The book prints no upgrade sentence for this class, so no hand_to_hand block is stored, and a pairing shows the race''s block. || JUDGEMENT - R.C.C. SKILLS IN A PAIRING: the race''s named and choice skills (the three specialty skills and two related skills, W.P. Assault Rifle, the Earth language) are unioned into a Battlemaster by the pairing rule. The book does not say whether a Battlemaster keeps the ordinary Fallam''s technical training or replaces it; stored as the app composes it. || RELATED: seven, plus one at levels 3, 5, 7, 10, 12 and 14. Communications +10, Espionage +10, Military +10, Physical +5 where applicable, Pilot +10, Pilot Related +10, Rogue +5, Technical +5, Wilderness +5; Domestic, Electrical, Mechanical, Science and W.P. any; Medical Paramedic or First Aid only. These replace the race''s ten in a pairing (related allowances are the occupation''s). Secondary: six, same limits without bonuses. || EQUIPMENT: Standard Equipment prints the race''s TB-Prime or FR-5 rifle, energy weapon of choice and modified Arkhon Body Armor (110 M.D.C.) again, plus a Tri-blade energy sword and a survival kit. The race''s three entries already arrive in a pairing, so only the two additions are stored (catalog tri-blade-energy-sword and survival-kit). Mission-issue extra equipment is prose. || MONEY: 2D6x1000 Arkhon credits, stored as 2d6x1000. class-check warns that a race stating its own starting_money would keep it; the Fallam R.C.C. prints and states none, so this one applies in the only pairing race_restrictions allows. Not supersedes_race: the book does not say the character stops being Fallam. || Cybernetics: none, a restriction."
