## Lore

Fallam legend says that a handful of ancient warriors touched the spirits and
gods of war and learned to call on them in battle - the Art of the Battle
Trance. Before the Arkhons came, the peaceful Fallam let the art all but die
out. The Arkhons, though, were dazzled by the few masters left, some of whom
could tear power armor apart barehanded, and after the conquest they gave them
honor their own people had denied them. The Battlemasters have been among the
Arkhons'' firmest supporters ever since.

Today they are an elite corps. Only about 1,500 serve in South America, and
they fight in their own three-to-six-warrior units called Talons rather than in
ordinary formations. Talons are sent against the enemy''s elite - True Incas,
Inca Warriors, dragons - and on sabotage, demolition and assassination
missions, often beside Spectral Hunter squads and ESP Specialist teams, with a
fierce and sometimes costly rivalry among the three.

## GM Notes

Rumor speaks of an Inner Circle of the oldest and best Battlemasters that has
worked in secret since the conquest to bring the Arkhons down. Most people
treat it as a fairy tale.
